    <item>
      <title>How ‘Come From Away’ Became a Lasting 9/11 Story</title>
      <link>https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/04/theater/come-from-away-musical-gander-canada.html</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/04/theater/come-from-away-musical-gander-canada.html</guid>
      <atom:link href="https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/04/theater/come-from-away-musical-gander-canada.html" rel="standout"></atom:link>
      <description>“Come From Away,” about a remote Newfoundland community that embraced grounded travelers, is playing all over the world — even in the town where it takes place.</description>
      <dc:creator>Michael Paulson and Johnny C.Y. Lam</dc:creator>
      <pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2026 12:24:37 +0000</pubDate>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Theater (Broadway)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">Theater</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_ttl">Come From Away (Play)</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Hein, David</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/nyt_per">Sankoff, Irene</category>
      <category domain="http://www.nytimes.com/namespaces/keywords/des">September 11 (2001)</category>
      <media:content height="1800" medium="image" url="https://static01.nyt.com/images/2026/09/13/multimedia/13cul-come-away-gander-07-bqwv/13cul-come-away-gander-07-bqwv-mediumSquareAt3X.jpg" width="1800"></media:content>
      <media:description>One of the show’s musical motifs and slogans is “You Are Here,” alluding to language used on locator maps. The words take on new meaning in Gander, since that’s where the show takes place.</media:description>
    </item>
